# CONSULT-72 (Cursor angle) — Offline vs connected predicate enumeration

Scope: object creation → `endBaselines` / `addToWorld` → `ClientWorld::*Notification::addToWorld` → `ms_tangibleSphereTree.addObject`. Only predicates whose **evaluated value differs** between (a) offline `setSinglePlayer(true)` + `Game::setScene(true,…)` and (b) live-server scene entry are listed. Same-value gates are omitted.

Legend: **(a)** = offline single-player scene; **(b)** = server-connected scene.

---

## 0. Global mode flag (upstream of everything)

| File:line | Predicate (as written) | (a) | (b) | Behaviour change |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `engine_advertise.cpp:331` | `Game::setSinglePlayer(true)` before load | executed | not executed | Sets `Game::ms_singlePlayer` true for entire offline session |
| `SwgCuiLoginScreen.cpp:434` | `Game::setSinglePlayer(false)` on login proceed | not reached (offline shim bypasses login) | executed | Clears single-player before avatar/cluster flow |
| `Game.h:322-324` / `Game.cpp:403` | `Game::getSinglePlayer()` → `ms_singlePlayer` | **true** | **false** | Every downstream `getSinglePlayer()` branch below |

