## 2. WorldSnapshot load / parse / proximity index (`ms_sphereTree`)

| File:line | Predicate (as written) | (a) | (b) | Behaviour change |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `WorldSnapshot.cpp:224` | `if (!Game::getSinglePlayer() \|\| !ConfigClientGame::getWorldSnapshotIgnorePobChanges())` before POB CRC check | **false** short-circuit if `getWorldSnapshotIgnorePobChanges()` true → CRC skipped | **true** (first clause) → CRC enforced unless config overrides | Failed CRC → `instantiateObject` returns 0 / `CEC_mismatchedPobCrc` (`WorldSnapshot.cpp:236-237`); object never created |
| `WorldSnapshot.cpp:1034-1037` | `if ( isSinglePlayer \|\| isInSet(ms_buildoutObjects, node->getNetworkIdInt()) == false \|\| ( node->getPortalLayoutCrc() == 0 && node->getContainedByNetworkIdInt() == 0 ) )` before `ms_sphereTree.addObject(node)` | **true** for all nodes (`isSinglePlayer` true) | **false** for buildout POB nodes in `ms_buildoutObjects` (inserted at `WorldSnapshot.cpp:948`) unless top-level non-portal exception | (b) buildout buildings are **excluded** from snapshot proximity tree; (a) they are **included**. Determines which nodes `WorldSnapshot::update` can create via `ms_sphereTree.findInRange` (`WorldSnapshot.cpp:1217`) |
| `WorldSnapshot.cpp:1195-1196` | `if (ms_parsePending) return;` in `update()` | same mechanism; timing may differ | same | No snapshot creates until parse completes — affects when buildings first become eligible |
| `WorldSnapshot.cpp:257-261` | `if (NetworkIdManager::getObjectById(...) != 0)` in `createObject` | false on first create | false on first create; **true** if snapshot object already replaced by server copy | Returns `CEC_objectAlreadyExists`, object not created, sphere handle stripped (`WorldSnapshot.cpp:1373-1375`) |
| `WorldSnapshot.cpp:285` | `object->setClientCached()` | always executed for snapshot creates | same for snapshot creates | Marks object `isClientCached()==true` (`ClientObject.cpp:1416-1418`) |
| `WorldSnapshot.cpp:606-614` | `bool const serverOwnedRoot = (clientObject != 0) && !ContainerInterface::isClientCachedOnly(*clientObject); if (serverOwnedRoot) … else delete object` in `unload()` | **false** for snapshot-only roots (all client-cached) | **true** for server-streamed roots still live during in-place reload | (b) can skip deleting live server objects on snapshot unload; (a) always deletes client-cached roots |
| `ContainerInterface.cpp:553-554` | `if (!clientObject->isClientCached()) return false;` inside `isClientCachedOnly` | snapshot tree: all cached → true | server NPC in cell → false | Drives unload guard above and delete drain below |
| `WorldSnapshot.cpp:1462-1469` | `if (ContainerInterface::isClientCachedOnly(*safe_cast<ClientObject*>(object))` in update delete drain | true → delete allowed | false (server-owned subtree) → **no delete** | (b) prevents snapshot-driven deletion of server-populated buildings |

