## 6. `ClientWorld` spatial registration (`ms_tangibleSphereTree`)

These gates are **identical code** in both modes; values differ only if upstream state differs.

| File:line | Predicate (as written) | (a) typical POB | (b) typical POB | Behaviour change |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ClientWorld.cpp:382` | `if ((!object.isChildObject()) && (object.getSpatialSubdivisionHandle() == 0))` in `TangibleNotification::addToWorld` | must both be true to register | same | If false, **no** `ms_tangibleSphereTree.addObject` — yields `candidates=0` at `ClientWorld.cpp:1656` |
| `Object.cpp:1072-1076` | `if (m_inWorld) return;` in `Object::addToWorld` | false first call | false first call | Early return prevents notification dispatch |
| `Object.cpp:1091` | `m_notificationList->addToWorld(*this)` | dispatches all notifications | same | Only path into `TangibleNotification::addToWorld` |

No `getSinglePlayer()` predicate exists in `ClientWorld.cpp` registration itself.

