## 10. NetworkId validity at cell-resolution time (downstream of creation, not creation itself)

| File:line | Predicate (as written) | (a) snapshot POB | (b) server/streamed POB | Behaviour change |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ClientWorld.cpp:1723` | `if (containingCellId.isValid())` in `findClosestCellObjectFromWorldPosition` | valid if cell owner got id from snapshot `setNetworkId` (`WorldSnapshot.cpp:287`) | valid from server baselines | Probe `rejectedForId` path; evidence says `rejectedForId=0` so **not the active failure mode** |
| `ClientObject.cpp:296-298` | fake NetworkId for cell objects created before scene | cells created as snapshot children get real ids from node, not fake-id path | server cells from baselines | Cell `NetworkId` validity depends on create path, not single-player flag at probe time |

